# Plugin UI (`ui.html`)

- No `figma` global — only `parent.postMessage` to reach the main thread.
- Wrap payloads as `{ pluginMessage: { ... } }` so the main thread receives them on `figma.ui.onmessage`.
- **Network**: remote requests only work for domains allowed in `manifest.json` → `networkAccess.allowedDomains`.
- Keep scripts compatible with the iframe environment Figma provides; avoid assuming full browser extension APIs unless documented for plugins.
- For user actions (buttons, inputs), post messages with a clear `type` field matching what `code.ts` handles.
